== Effects ==
* +2 flat [[damage]] to tears fired from Isaac's left eye.

== Notes ==
* The damage bonus is unaffected by both positive and negative damage multipliers.
* {{C|Cain}} has a 50% chance of firing a shot with the effects of Chemical Peel whenever he fires.
* {{i|Blood Clot}} applies to the same eye and the effects stack.
** Generally every interaction and synergy that applies to Chemical Peel also applies to Blood Clot. See its page for any differences to what is listed here.

== Synergies ==
* {{i|20/20}}/{{i|The Inner Eye}}/{{i|Mutant Spider}}: Every other set of tears has the Chemical Peel effect.
* {{i|Brimstone}}: The entire laser has a high chance to have the Chemical Peel effect, with no visual difference.
* {{i|Dr. Fetus}}: The damage bonus applies to every bomb, with no visual difference.
* {{i|Epic Fetus}}: The missiles have a high chance to deal 40 points extra damage, with no visual difference.
* {{i|Lead Pencil}}: All tears in the tear barrage will gain the Chemical Peel effect.
* {{i|The Ludovico Technique}}: The tear flashes between normal and the higher-damaging Chemical Peel tear.
* {{i|Mom's Knife}}: Each tick of the Knife's damage has a high chance to gain the bonus, with no visual difference.
* {{I|Soy Milk}} / {{i|Almond Milk}}: Chemical Peel is unaffected by the damage down modifier, greatly increasing DPS.
* {{i|Tech.5}}: Chemical Peel has a chance to apply to the laser, with no visual difference.
* {{i|Technology}}: Lasers have a high chance to gain extra damage, with no visual difference.
* {{i|Technology 2}}: Every tear fired has Chemical Peel applied to it, but the laser is unaffected.

== Interactions ==
* {{i|Diplopia}}: No effect from additional copies.
* {{i|Incubus}}: Has a 50% chance of firing a shot with the Chemical Peel effect.
* {{i|Sad Bombs}}: The last type of tear fired is used for the burst.
* {{i|Stapler}}: Gives a 50% chance of firing a Chemical Peel shot, similar to Cain.
* {{i|Tech X}}: Overrides Chemical Peel.
* {{i|Varicose Veins}}: The last type of tear fired is used for the burst.

